Head-test maps, unary numerals, and Peano axioms on the sequence domain.
<!-- formalization -->
**Definition (`headValC`).** Head-test evaluation on strings for cone versus singleton branches.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Theorem (`headValC_nil`).** Head-test on the empty string returns the default.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Theorem (`headValC_false`).** Head-test on a false prefix returns the first branch.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Theorem (`headValC_true`).** Head-test on a true prefix returns the second branch.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Definition (`T`).** The two-element token domain for sequence values.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Theorem (`headValC_bot_le`).** Head-test on bottom prefixes is monotone in the prefix order.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Theorem (`not_cone_subset_singleton`).** A cone neighbourhood is never contained in a singleton.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Theorem (`cone_ne_singleton`).** Cone and singleton neighbourhoods are distinct.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Definition (`liftC`).** Universal approximable map from the sequence domain using head-test values.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Definition (`emptyMap`).** Constant false head-tests with bottom on cones.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Theorem (`liftC_strBot`).** The lift sends stratum bottoms to cone values.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Theorem (`liftC_strElem`).** The lift sends stratum elements to singleton values.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Theorem (`emptyMap_strElem`).** Empty map values on stratum elements.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Theorem (`emptyMap_strBot`).** Empty map values on stratum bottoms.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Definition (`oneMap`).** Map sending cones to bottom/false/true pattern.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Definition (`zeroMap`).** Map with true on singleton tails and mixed cones.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Theorem (`zeroMap_strElem`).** Zero map on stratum elements.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Theorem (`zeroMap_strBot`).** Zero map on stratum bottoms.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Theorem (`oneMap_strElem`).** One map on stratum elements.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Theorem (`oneMap_strBot`).** One map on stratum bottoms.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Definition (`oneDef`).** Fixed-point-style definition of the numeral one map.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Theorem (`condT_bot`).** Conditional with bottom first argument is bottom.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Theorem (`one_def_strBot`).** The simple one map agrees with the fixed-point definition on stratum bottoms.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Theorem (`one_def_strElem`).** The simple one map agrees with the fixed-point definition on stratum elements.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Theorem (`peano_cons_disjoint`).** Prefixes false and true yield distinct strings.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Theorem (`peano_cons_injective`).** Equality of conses implies equality of tails.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Theorem (`peano_induction`).** Induction on finite bit-strings.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
**Theorem (`peano_nil_ne_cons`).** The empty string is not a cons.

*Proof.* As in the formal module. ∎
